# Prfy: debits accumulate into one LimitedCredit allowance within a transaction.
#
# The original unit test /limited-credit-transaction-state only reached the
# saturating branch of the accumulation (INT32_MAX plus 1), and every other debit
# was a single debit per transaction, so a mutant that replaced the running
# allowance with the latest debit amount (pending = amount instead of
# pending += amount) survived both the unit test and the vector. This vector
# pins the additive behaviour: two debits (3 and 4) in one transaction give an
# allowance of 7, visible to LimitedCredit in the same transaction and, once
# committed, to GetFileSettings.
#
# Responses were recorded from the reference engine and cross-checked by hand:
# 50 - 3 - 4 + 7 = 50 (0x32), and 50 - 3 - 4 = 43 (0x2B).

name: LimitedCredit allowance accumulates across debits
case-id: prfy-limited-credit-debit-accumulates
origin: synthetic
feature-version: 6
source: tests/test_dfc_virtual_picc_value_vectors.c#/limited-credit-transaction-state
uid: 0476616C756531
picc-generation: EV3
picc-storage: 4096

